# Death to Our Enemies' divided damage when one of its two targets becomes illegal (CR 608.2b): Bot1 puts the fourth plan
# counter on it with Mox Emerald on turn 3 and divides the 7 as 5 to Bot2 and 2 to Bot2's Ornithopter. In response Bot1
# Lightning Bolts the Ornithopter itself. The reflexive ability still resolves for its legal target - Bot2 takes the 5 it
# was given - and the Ornithopter's 2 are dealt to nobody. The Bolt, a noncreature spell, triggers nothing: the
# enchantment was sacrificed.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Black Lotus
Death to Our Enemies
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Mox Emerald
Lightning Bolt
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x19

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Hand.Death to Our Enemies.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Divide(Bot2: 5; Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter: 2)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
? Stack.Count = 3
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 15
Bot2.Graveyard = Ornithopter
Bot1.Graveyard = Lightning Bolt; Death to Our Enemies; Black Lotus
Bot1.Battlefield = Mountain; Mox Pearl; Mox Sapphire; Mox Jet; Mox Emerald; Treasure Token; Treasure Token; Treasure Token; Treasure Token
